# Helion Particle Lab environment variables
#
# The app runs with ZERO env vars locally: it falls back to an embedded
# PGLite (Postgres-in-WASM) database that needs no configuration. Copy this
# file to `.env` only when you want to point at a real database or turn on
# authentication for a hosted deploy.

# DATABASE_URL (optional locally, RECOMMENDED for deploys)
# Postgres connection string. When set, the app (src/lib/db.ts) and the
# build-time migrator (scripts/migrate.mjs) use hosted Postgres instead of
# the embedded PGLite fallback. Any pg-compatible provider works; a free
# Neon database is the easiest to create from a phone.
# IMPORTANT: without DATABASE_URL the app still runs, but PGLite storage is
# in-memory and does NOT persist across serverless invocations, so any data
# is lost between requests on a hosted deploy. Set this for real persistence.
# DATABASE_URL="postgres://user:password@host:5432/dbname?sslmode=require"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Authentication (NOT available on a plain standalone deploy)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The particle simulator runs fully WITHOUT authentication, and that is the
# supported standalone mode: the core sim has no auth dependency, so nothing
# below is required to run or deploy the app.
#
# The built-in sign-in (src/lib/auth/server.ts) federates to a shared "Grok
# auth broker". Real federated sign-in is gated on the broker credentials
# GROK_AUTH_CLIENT_ID + GROK_AUTH_CLIENT_SECRET (and GROK_AUTH_ISSUER). This
# standalone template does NOT provide those, and it cannot mint them, so
# federated sign-in is NOT available on a plain Vercel deploy unless you wire
# up your own auth broker to supply them.
#
# Notes on the individual variables (documented for completeness):
#
# VITE_AUTH_ENABLED
#   This is only ever read as an OFF switch: the code does
#   `env("VITE_AUTH_ENABLED") === "false"`. Setting it to "true" does NOT by
#   itself enable working sign-in; leaving it unset behaves the same as "true".
#   Set it to "false" to force auth off everywhere.
# VITE_AUTH_ENABLED="false"

# BETTER_AUTH_SECRET
#   Genuinely read to sign auth sessions
#   (secret: env("BETTER_AUTH_SECRET") ?? previewAuthSecret()). Set it for a
#   stable signing secret across restarts, but note it is NOT sufficient on its
#   own to produce working federated sign-in (that still needs the GROK_AUTH_*
#   broker credentials above). Generate your own value with:
#     openssl rand -hex 32
#   Do NOT reuse the placeholder below; paste your own generated secret.
# BETTER_AUTH_SECRET="replace-with-output-of-openssl-rand-hex-32"

# BETTER_AUTH_URL
#   The public base URL of your deployment, used for auth callbacks. Only
#   relevant if you have wired up broker credentials. On Vercel this is your
#   project URL, e.g. https://your-app.vercel.app
# BETTER_AUTH_URL="https://your-app.vercel.app"
